{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/8z6eoa","slide":1,"text":"Pitch cue: The current AnnSetu implementation uses a single pnpm monorepo with a Next.js PWA and a NestJS platform core. PostgreSQL handles transactional records, Redis supports cache, rate limits and realtime distribution, and BullMQ processes outbox jobs with retry and dead-letter handling.\n\nFarmer journey: capacity planning, login or assisted verification, atomic slot booking, queue tracking, gate entry, weighing and quality inspection, lot decision, then settlement. Assisted bookings can be tracked without an account using the mobile or token number.\n\nPayment rule: registered farmers may follow the PFMS/DBT-compatible simulated path. Assistant bookings do not collect verified bank details and therefore allow cash settlement only.\n\nEvidence: docs/pitch_deck/FEATURE_VALIDATION_CURRENT_CODEBASE.md; apps/web/package.json; apps/api/package.json; apps/api/src/modules/booking/booking.controller.ts; apps/api/src/modules/queue/queue.service.ts; apps/api/src/modules/payments/payment-policy.ts; apps/web/src/screens/PublicBookingTracking.tsx; apps/web/src/screens/CenterDashboard.tsx.\n\nQualification: government, SMS, USSD, IVR and translation integrations use adapter-ready mocks or local fallbacks in the SIH demo. No version numbers appear on the slide by request."}